---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { SUPPORT_EMAIL } from '../consts';

const title = 'Privacy Policy — Bible Crossword Challenge';
const description =
  'Bible Crossword Challenge privacy policy. No account required. Progress stays on your device and syncs privately through your own iCloud. Only anonymous usage and crash analytics.';
---
<Layout title={title} description={description} path="/privacy/">
  <main id="main" class="page">
    <div class="wrap" style="max-width:720px">
      <p class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span>Privacy</p>
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: 7 November 2026</p>

      <div class="content-section prose" style="max-width:none">
        <h2>The short version</h2>
        <p>Bible Crossword Challenge is offline-first. You don't need an account. Your puzzle progress, streaks, and achievements are stored on your device and, if you're signed in to iCloud, synced between your own devices through your private iCloud account. We can't see that data.</p>

        <h2>iCloud sync</h2>
        <p>Sync uses Apple's CloudKit private database, which belongs to your Apple Account. Only your devices can read it; it never passes through a server of ours. Turn it off any time in Settings › [your name] › iCloud.</p>

        <h2>Information we collect</h2>
        <p>We do not collect personal information such as your name, email, or contacts. We use anonymous analytics and crash reporting (via Google Firebase and PostHog) to understand how the app is used and to fix problems. This may include:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Anonymous usage events (e.g. a puzzle was opened or completed)</li>
          <li>Device type, OS version, and app version</li>
          <li>Crash and performance diagnostics</li>
          <li>Whether a launch is a first install or an update, so we can tell new players from returning ones</li>
        </ul>
        <p>These events are tied to a random identifier, not to you. We do not record your screen, and we do not track you across other apps or websites.</p>

        <h2>Purchases</h2>
        <p>Premium is sold through Apple's App Store using StoreKit. Apple processes all payments — we never receive your card or billing details. RevenueCat checks which subscription is active, using an anonymous app identifier and Apple's purchase receipts. We record which plan was bought, its price, and whether it started as a free trial, so we can tell trials apart from paid subscriptions.</p>

        <h2>Game Center</h2>
        <p>The weekly mini leaderboard uses Apple Game Center. If you're signed in to Game Center, your Game Center nickname and solve time appear on that leaderboard. It's optional, and Apple handles it under its own privacy policy.</p>

        <h2>Third-party services</h2>
        <p>We use Google Firebase (Analytics), PostHog (product analytics), RevenueCat (subscription status), and Apple (App Store, StoreKit, iCloud, Game Center, and on-device crash diagnostics). PostHog data is processed on their EU cloud. Their handling of data is governed by their own privacy policies:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Firebase Privacy</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://posthog.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PostHog Privacy</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://www.revenuecat.com/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">RevenueCat Privacy</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Apple Privacy</a></li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>The app does not knowingly collect personal information from children. No personal data is required to use it.</p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>We may update this policy from time to time. Material changes will be reflected on this page with a new “last updated” date.</p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions? Email <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
